# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# Deliberate divergence from bd's defaults (owner decision 2026-08-01).
# bd tracks .beads/interactions.jsonl by design — it is absent from
# .beads/.gitignore, which is what makes it tracked. In this repo it is a
# local audit log that every bd command rewrites, so it sat permanently dirty
# and got excluded from commit after commit by hand. Untracked instead.
#
# Kept HERE rather than in .beads/.gitignore because bd owns that file and may
# rewrite it on upgrade or `bd doctor --fix`. If a bd command re-adds this to
# the index, that is the divergence being undone, not a new file appearing.
.beads/interactions.jsonl

# `bd backup init` (shotwright-2sr.3) writes the backup destination here as an
# ABSOLUTE PATH INCLUDING THE OPERATOR USERNAME, and bd does not ignore it. This
# repository is headed public, and the tarball leak gate would NOT catch it —
# that gate scans the packed tarball, and .beads/ is not in `files`. So the
# ignore has to live here. If a bd upgrade starts ignoring these itself, this
# becomes redundant rather than wrong.
.beads/dolt-backup.json
.beads/dolt-backup-state.json
# bd worktree
worktrees/shotwright-746.18.4/
